From: Anze <aanzdev@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] screensaver: add dedicated "oled" anti-image-retention type

Add a new "oled" value to the SCREENSAVER TYPE list, alongside dim/black/
random video/slideshow/suspend.

Until now the compositor-level OLED anti-image-retention overlay (the oledsaver
package) was paired with the stock "black" screensaver type, which was
confusing: selecting "black" both made the screen look off AND launched the
sweeping pixel-refresh overlay. "oled" is now its own entry, so plain "black"
stays a plain black screen and "oled" is the dedicated burn-in-protection mode.

No SystemScreenSaver change is needed: "oled" is not video/slideshow/suspend,
so startScreenSaver() falls through to the standard STATE_SCREENSAVER_ACTIVE
path (static screen, no media); renderScreenSaver() draws opaque black for any
non-"dim" behavior; and Scripting::fireEvent("screensaver-start", behavior) /
"screensaver-stop" already fire for every type. The oledsaver screensaver-start
hook is repointed from "black" to "oled" in its own package.

The French translation is provided ("OLED (anti-rémanence)") so the option is
not shown as untranslated English in the FR UI; other locales fall back to the
"oled" term (universal). msgmerge -U --no-fuzzy-matching preserves the added
translation at build time.

---
diff --git a/es-app/src/guis/GuiGeneralScreensaverOptions.cpp b/es-app/src/guis/GuiGeneralScreensaverOptions.cpp
index d64c8c4..e0ed888 100644
--- a/es-app/src/guis/GuiGeneralScreensaverOptions.cpp
+++ b/es-app/src/guis/GuiGeneralScreensaverOptions.cpp
@@ -13,6 +13,7 @@
 
 #define fake_gettext_dim			_("dim")
 #define fake_gettext_black			_("black")
+#define fake_gettext_oled			_("oled")
 #define fake_gettext_randomvideo	_("random video")
 #define fake_gettext_slideshow		_("slideshow")
 #define fake_gettext_suspend		_("suspend")
@@ -44,10 +45,15 @@ GuiGeneralScreensaverOptions::GuiGeneralScreensaverOptions(Window* window, int s
 	// Screensaver behavior
 	auto ctlBehavior = std::make_shared< OptionListComponent<std::string> >(mWindow, _("SCREENSAVER TYPE"), false);
 
+	// "oled" is a dedicated anti-image-retention screensaver: ES draws a static
+	// black screen (handled exactly like "black") and fires screensaver-start/
+	// -stop, while the compositor-level oledsaver overlay paints a sweeping
+	// pixel-refresh band on top. Kept separate from "black" so plain "black"
+	// stays a plain black screen.
 	if (ApiSystem::getInstance()->isScriptingSupported(ApiSystem::SUSPEND))
-		ctlBehavior->addRange({ "dim", "black", "random video", "slideshow", "suspend" }, ssBehavior);
+		ctlBehavior->addRange({ "dim", "black", "oled", "random video", "slideshow", "suspend" }, ssBehavior);
 	else
-		ctlBehavior->addRange({ "dim", "black", "random video", "slideshow" }, ssBehavior);
+		ctlBehavior->addRange({ "dim", "black", "oled", "random video", "slideshow" }, ssBehavior);
 
 	addWithLabel(_("SCREENSAVER TYPE"), ctlBehavior, selectItem == 1);
 	ctlBehavior->setSelectedChangedCallback([this](const std::string& name)
diff --git a/locale/lang/fr/LC_MESSAGES/emulationstation2.po b/locale/lang/fr/LC_MESSAGES/emulationstation2.po
index 34cf203..f5e55ce 100644
--- a/locale/lang/fr/LC_MESSAGES/emulationstation2.po
+++ b/locale/lang/fr/LC_MESSAGES/emulationstation2.po
@@ -1648,6 +1648,9 @@ msgstr "écran assombri"
 msgid "black"
 msgstr "écran noir"
 
+msgid "oled"
+msgstr "OLED (anti-rémanence)"
+
 msgid "random video"
 msgstr "vidéo"
 
